    feat(gitreins): verdict-coverage audit guard (INT-GATE-2)
    
    Adds a standing audit for the complete-without-verdict defect class in the
    gitreins lifecycle state: scripts/gitreins_verdict_audit.py fails (exit 1)
    when a task sits in_progress past --stale-days (default 14) with no
    verdict.json naming it (ORPHAN-STALE), or flips to complete inside the
    --window-days (default 30) window with no verdict and no exception entry
    (ORPHAN-NOVERDICT). Malformed verdicts are counted and skipped; unparseable
    dates are unknown-age and never fail; cap_hits counts in-window "Iteration
    cap" verdict bodies as a WARN-only signal. .gitreins/verdict_audit_exceptions.yaml
    exempts DF-AIPP-13-R3 (judge in flight at tick-386 closeout, closed partial,
    residual DF-AIPP-13-R4 filed). 14 unit tests on synthetic tmp_path repos
    only.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
